  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 140 AM EDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nConditions will remain wet and unsettled through the extended period \nas South Florida remains entrenched in an area of weakness between \ntwo ridges, and the upper level trough causing this weakness extends \nsouth across the Appalachian ridge. At the same time, some of the\nensemble suites are hinting at a few tropical upper tropospheric \ntroughs (TUTTs) meandering across our region, which could enhance\ninstability and lift and result in more widespread unsettled \nweather. In fact, the NBM is picking up on this possibility as we \nhead into the weekend, with Friday afternoon potentially being one\nof the wetter ones in the entire forecast period (with 60-80% \nchances of rainfall and QPF in the 1-2 inch range), and activity\nbeing maximized across the interior and southwest portions of \nSouth Florida. With the potential for more widespread coverage, \nand the added support from features aloft, the heavy rainfall \ncould lead to localized flooding for portions of southwest FL. \nWe'll continue to monitor this potential solution and see how \nmodels trend as the week progresses. \n\nRidging looks likely to start building back over the weekend and \nas we head into next week. Temperatures should remain in the low \nto mid 90s each afternoon.",
